oryLoader``.  Uses the DietGPU raw ANS codec\\n(exponent-only compression + raw sign|mantissa storage) for BF16 KV cache\\nblocks.\\n\\nInterface parity with ZipServCompressor's KV methods (the subset that is\\nexercised from ``DualMemoryLoader``, ``kv_offload_system`` and\\n``v1_cuda_graph_wrapper``):\\n\\n- ``batch_decomp_stream`` attribute\\n- ``warmup_kv_buffers(block_shape, max_n_blocks, n_layers, ...)``\\n- ``init_kv_compress_workers(n_workers, max_blocks, n_layers)``\\n- ``compress_batch_async(layer_id, block_ids, gpu_k, gpu_v)``\\n- ``wait_compress_async(layer_id, block_shape, timeout_sec)``\\n- ``stop_kv_compress_workers()``\\n- ``has_compressed_kv(layer_id)`` / ``_compressed_kv`` dict\\n- ``has_persistent_compressed_kv(layer_id, block_ids)``\\n- ``decompress_batch(layer_id, block_ids, output_buffers=(k_cache, v_cache))``\\n- ``free_persistent_block(layer_id, block_id)``\\n\\nUnlike ZipServ, there is no C++ worker thread pool — DietGPU compresses\\nentirely on GPU, so ``compress_batch_async`` simply launches the\\ncompress + D2H pipeline on an internal CUDA stream and ``wait_compress_async``\\nsynchronises it.\\n\\nStorage layout (per layer, per K and V):\\n  - ``comp_exp`` : pinned [max_n_blocks, max_comp_size] uint8 row-major by\\n    physical slot.  Actual per-block payload length tracked in ``exp_sizes``.\\n  - ``sm``       : pinned [max_n_blocks, block_bytes] uint8 row-major by\\n    physical slot.\\n  - ``exp_sizes``: pinned [max_n_blocks] int32 — per-slot compressed size.\\n  - ``_kv_slot`` : block_id -> physical slot.  Slots [0, active_count) are\\n    kept dense via eager swap-with-last on free.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport logging\\nimport os\\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport torch\\n\\nfrom tiered_serve.compressor_base import TensorCompressor\\nfrom tiered_serve.tensor_compressor import _ensure_dietgpu_loaded\\n\\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\\n\\n\\n# DietGPU ANS worst-case compressed size for a batch of equal-size inputs.\\n# Mirrors ``getMaxCompressedSize`` from dietgpu/ans/GpuANSEncode.cu which is\\n# roughly ``overhead + max_block_size_coalesced * ceil(N / 4096)`` where each\\n# 4096-byte block can expand to ~2x of its input in the coalesced layout.\\n# Use a conservative bound of ``2 * N + 16 KiB`` rounded to 128 B.\\ndef _max_comp_size(uncompressed_bytes: int) -> int:\\n    size = uncompressed_bytes * 2 + 16 * 1024\\n    return (size + 127) & ~127\\n\\n\\nclass DietGPUKVCompressor(TensorCompressor):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"DietGPU-based KV cache compressor.\\n\\n    Inherits :class:`TensorCompressor` so that\\n    :class:`tiered_serve.dual_memory_loader.DualMemoryLoader` can hold\\n    ``weight_compressor`` and ``kv_compressor`` as uniformly-typed\\n    :class:`TensorCompressor` instances.\\n\\n    The single-tensor weight API (``compress`` / ``decompress`` /\\n    ``compress_batch`` / ``decompress_batch``) is **not** implemented —\\n    this backend is KV-only and exposes its work through KV-specific\\n    batch methods (``compress_batch_async`` / ``wait_compress_async`` /\\n    ``decompress_batch``).  Calls to the weight API raise\\n    :class:`NotImplementedError`.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, comp_stream: torch.cuda.Stream,\\n                 workspace_bytes: int = 384 * 1024 * 1024):\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Abstract base class for weight tensor compressors.\\n\\nEvery concrete compressor in :mod:`tiered_serve.tensor_compressor`\\n(``UBLBCompressor``, ``ZipServCompressor``, ``DietGPUCompressor``,\\n``DietGPUFP8Compressor``, ``ZipServFP8GpuCompressor``) inherits from\\n:class:`TensorCompressor` defined here.\\n\\nShared infrastructure provided by the base class:\\n\\n* ``self.comp_stream`` — per-instance CUDA stream for compress /\\n  decompress.  Created on the current device when the caller does not\\n  supply one (and ``None`` on CPU-only hosts).\\n* :func:`TensorCompressor._jit_load_ext` — thin wrapper around\\n  :func:`torch.utils.cpp_extension.load` that resolves source paths\\n  under ``cpp_extensions/csrc`` so subclasses do not have to repeat\\n  the same ``os.path.join(__file__, \\\"..\\\", ...)`` boilerplate.\\n* :func:`TensorCompressor._log_compress_ratio` — uniform info-level log\\n  line for compress operations.\\n\\nThe :class:`CompressedTensor` :class:`typing.Protocol` documents (and,\\nunder ``isinstance`` checks, validates) the structural interface every\\n``Compressed*Tensor`` class exposes to consumers.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport logging\\nimport os\\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\\nfrom typing import Any, Iterable, Optional, Protocol, runtime_checkable\\n\\nimport torch\\n\\n\\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\\n\\n\\n@runtime_checkable\\nclass CompressedTensor(Protocol):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Structural protocol satisfied by every ``Compressed*Tensor`` class.\\n\\n    Attributes:\\n        output_tensor: Optional pre-allocated decompress destination.\\n\\n    Properties:\\n        total_compressed_size: Total bytes occupied by the compressed\\n            payload(s).  Used for ratio logging and slot accounting.\\n        nbytes: Alias for total_compressed_size where applicable.\\n\\n    Methods:\\n        to(device): Return a copy of the compressed payload(s) staged on\\n            the requested device (or update internal GPU buffers in place\\n            for compressors that support it).\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    output_tensor: Optional[torch.Tensor]\\n\\n    @property\\n    def total_compressed_size(self) -> int: ...  # pragma: no cover\\n\\n    def to(self, device: Any) -> \\\"CompressedTensor\\\": ...  # pragma: no cover\\n\\n\\nclass TensorCompressor(ABC):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Abstract base class for weight tensor compressors.\\n\\n    Subclasses must implement :meth:`compress` and :meth:`decompress`.\\n    They may override :meth:`fused_mm` to provide a fused\\n    decompress + GEMM kernel